{"audit_run_id":"audit:f3d293f3b269421db181a36ac0f4c048","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":80,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"A hospital microbiology laboratory tested whether a hydrophilic surface coating"},{"end_column":75,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"reduces bacterial biofilm on urinary catheter material. Forty-four sterile"},{"end_column":78,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"silicone catheter coupons of identical size were prepared: 22 uncoated and 22"},{"end_column":73,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"with the hydrophilic coating. Each coupon was incubated on its own in an"},{"end_column":75,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"identical flow cell, with the same reference bacterial strain and the same"},{"end_column":81,"end_line":10,"start_column":1,"start_line":10,"text":"artificial urine medium, for 48 hours. Each coupon was then removed and measured"},{"end_column":39,"end_line":11,"start_column":1,"start_line":11,"text":"for the whole declared outcome family."},{"end_column":81,"end_line":13,"start_column":1,"start_line":13,"text":"Group sizes: 22 uncoated coupons and 22 hydrophilic-coated coupons, 44 in total."},{"end_column":75,"end_line":17,"start_column":1,"start_line":17,"text":"The data live in `biofilm_coupons.csv`. One row is one coupon, holding the"},{"end_column":80,"end_line":18,"start_column":1,"start_line":18,"text":"complete outcome family for that coupon; no coupon appears twice. Every cell is"},{"end_column":32,"end_line":19,"start_column":1,"start_line":19,"text":"filled, so there are no blanks."},{"end_column":35,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"| Column | Units | What it holds |"},{"end_column":20,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"| --- | --- | --- |"},{"end_column":77,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"| `coupon_id` | — | Coupon label, `CP-01` through `CP-44`, unique per row. |"},{"end_column":63,"end_line":24,"start_column":1,"start_line":24,"text":"| `surface` | — | Group, either `uncoated` or `hydrophilic`. |"},{"end_column":114,"end_line":25,"start_column":1,"start_line":25,"text":"| `biofilm_od590` | optical density at 590 nm | Declared outcome 1: biofilm biomass by crystal violet staining. |"},{"end_column":122,"end_line":26,"start_column":1,"start_line":26,"text":"| `viable_log10_cfu_per_cm2` | log10 CFU per cm^2 | Declared outcome 2: viable cells recovered from the coupon surface. |"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"| `thickness_um` | micrometres | Declared outcome 3: mean biofilm thickness by confocal imaging. |"},{"end_column":130,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"| `eps_protein_ug_per_cm2` | micrograms per cm^2 | Declared outcome 4: extracellular polymeric substance protein on the coupon. |"},{"end_column":76,"end_line":32,"start_column":1,"start_line":32,"text":"For each declared outcome, the two surfaces were compared with a two-sample"},{"end_column":77,"end_line":33,"start_column":1,"start_line":33,"text":"Welch t-test, which is the two-sample test for a continuous measurement that"},{"end_column":78,"end_line":34,"start_column":1,"start_line":34,"text":"does not assume the two groups share a variance. Each declared outcome is its"},{"end_column":70,"end_line":35,"start_column":1,"start_line":35,"text":"own scientific question and stands on its own. An outcome is declared"},{"end_column":70,"end_line":36,"start_column":1,"start_line":36,"text":"significantly affected by the coating when its p-value is below 0.05."},{"end_column":78,"end_line":40,"start_column":1,"start_line":40,"text":"Outcomes appear in the declared order. The difference is the hydrophilic mean"},{"end_column":78,"end_line":41,"start_column":1,"start_line":41,"text":"minus the uncoated mean, so a negative value means less biofilm on the coated"},{"end_column":9,"end_line":42,"start_column":1,"start_line":42,"text":"coupons."},{"end_column":89,"end_line":44,"start_column":1,"start_line":44,"text":"| Declared outcome | Uncoated mean | Hydrophilic mean | Difference | p-value | Verdict |"},{"end_column":38,"end_line":45,"start_column":1,"start_line":45,"text":"| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |"},{"end_column":80,"end_line":46,"start_column":1,"start_line":46,"text":"| 1. Biofilm biomass (OD590) | 0.980 | 0.460 | -0.520 | 2.7e-11 | significant |"},{"end_column":85,"end_line":47,"start_column":1,"start_line":47,"text":"| 2. Viable cells (log10 CFU/cm^2) | 6.420 | 6.030 | -0.391 | 0.0428 | significant |"},{"end_column":86,"end_line":48,"start_column":1,"start_line":48,"text":"| 3. Mean biofilm thickness (um) | 48.49 | 47.59 | -0.90 | 0.8274 | not significant |"},{"end_column":78,"end_line":49,"start_column":1,"start_line":49,"text":"| 4. EPS protein (ug/cm^2) | 27.50 | 15.84 | -11.66 | 6.9e-08 | significant |"},{"end_column":78,"end_line":53,"start_column":1,"start_line":53,"text":"- **Biofilm biomass (OD590).** The coating significantly affects this outcome"},{"end_column":80,"end_line":54,"start_column":3,"start_line":54,"text":"(p = 2.7e-11). Coated coupons carried about half the crystal violet signal of"},{"end_column":41,"end_line":55,"start_column":3,"start_line":55,"text":"uncoated coupons, 0.460 against 0.980."},{"end_column":76,"end_line":56,"start_column":1,"start_line":56,"text":"- **Viable cells (log10 CFU/cm^2).** The coating significantly affects this"},{"end_column":80,"end_line":57,"start_column":3,"start_line":57,"text":"outcome (p = 0.0428). Coated coupons yielded 0.39 log10 CFU/cm^2 fewer viable"},{"end_column":73,"end_line":58,"start_column":3,"start_line":58,"text":"cells, which is a small margin and sits just under the 0.05 threshold."},{"end_column":77,"end_line":59,"start_column":1,"start_line":59,"text":"- **Mean biofilm thickness (um).** The coating does not significantly affect"},{"end_column":81,"end_line":60,"start_column":3,"start_line":60,"text":"this outcome (p = 0.8274). The two surfaces were effectively the same, 47.6 um"},{"end_column":19,"end_line":61,"start_column":3,"start_line":61,"text":"against 48.5 um."},{"end_column":76,"end_line":62,"start_column":1,"start_line":62,"text":"- **EPS protein (ug/cm^2).** The coating significantly affects this outcome"},{"end_column":77,"end_line":63,"start_column":3,"start_line":63,"text":"(p = 6.9e-08). Coated coupons carried 11.7 ug/cm^2 less EPS protein, about"},{"end_column":38,"end_line":64,"start_column":3,"start_line":64,"text":"42 percent below the uncoated mean."},{"end_column":74,"end_line":66,"start_column":1,"start_line":66,"text":"Taken outcome by outcome, the coating cut biofilm biomass and EPS protein"},{"end_column":78,"end_line":67,"start_column":1,"start_line":67,"text":"clearly, cut viable counts by a small margin, and left mean biofilm thickness"},{"end_column":11,"end_line":68,"start_column":1,"start_line":68,"text":"unchanged."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:133e302b6982babdd0f5","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:aa2ad2f0cc0f887ea1fd02ef862e0d61440468cd1e83f11b3e8e813ac3783187","end_line":68,"locator":"report.md:1-68","path":"report.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
